# vault-demo-web – environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env, fill in your values, then either:
#   • Load it manually:  source .env  (Linux/macOS / Git Bash on Windows)
#   • Or use docker run --env-file .env ...
#   • Or use docker-compose (it picks up .env automatically)
#
# NOTE: This app does NOT connect to Vault directly.
#       Secrets are injected by Vault Agent (files) or the
#       Vault Secrets Operator (env vars / mounted K8s Secrets).
#
# When both a config file and environment variables are present,
# environment variables take precedence.

# ── Config file (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute or relative path to a YAML config file.
# If unset the app searches standard locations automatically.
# CONFIG_FILE=/etc/vault-demo/config.yaml

# ── Server settings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER_HOST=0.0.0.0
# SERVER_PORT=8080
# SERVER_DEBUG=false

# ── Secrets injection settings ──────────────────────────────────────
# Where to read injected secrets from:
#   file – Vault Agent rendered-template directory (see SECRETS_PATH)
#   env  – environment variables with a common prefix (see SECRETS_ENV_PREFIX)
#   both – read from both sources
SECRETS_SOURCE=file

# Directory where Vault Agent writes rendered secret files.
SECRETS_PATH=/vault/secrets

# Env-var prefix used by the Vault Secrets Operator.
# Example: if SECRETS_ENV_PREFIX=SECRET_ then SECRET_DB_PASSWORD is collected.
# SECRETS_ENV_PREFIX=SECRET_

# ── Example: secrets injected via env (Vault Secrets Operator) ──────
# SECRET_DB_PASSWORD=s3cr3t
# SECRET_API_KEY=my-api-key
